ime was overheard  struggling to keep a Contracting job  despite life's struggles he always found  time for Sarah whether it be a late  night movie watching session or  attending her weekend soccer games the  night of Joel's birthday 32nd in the  game and I believe 36th in the series  Sarah gifted him with a new watch to  replace his old broken one this later  becomes a treasured Memento to Joel  because of what happens on outbreak day  of which starts with their neighbor  Jimmy acting a bit strange and then  escalating to the full-on outbreak we  know during this night though Sarah Joel  and Tommy are trying to escape Austin  only to be caught in a horde of infected  leading to Joel and Sarah escaping but a  major turning point of Joel's life  occurs when a military officer thinks  that they are infected shooting them  resulting in Sarah being mortally  wounded Joel loses the one person he  truly loved and only the watch to  remember her by that's why he fondly  looks at it later even though it's  broken and doesn't work now this is  where the 20-year time Jump happens and  much of Joel's early kind of this life  in between is a mystery though through  brief conversations and other people we  meet along the way there's a general  idea of the character Joel was during  this time shortly after Sarah's death  Joel contemplated ending his own life  after seeing the chaos of what this new  world held but instead chose to survive  fighting alongside his brother Tommy  however in order to survive this took  the two down a dark path of torturing  and deceiving countless innocent people  essentially becoming a hunter these were  like parasitic Bandit type people that  threw any sort of moral code out the  window using any sort of trickery  tactics to Ambush others for their own  personal gain and survival Joel was able  to smuggle the pair into to Boston where  Joel spent most of his days until he was  eventually paired up with Ellie though  after years of seeing nightmares