 persuaded by Tess  into taking the job as they hit the road  however there's a huge snag when they  are stopped by military control  revealing that Ellie is actually  infected Joel and Tess are confused why  Marlene would set them up to transport  an infected but Ellie pleads with them  stating that her bite is more than three  weeks old she is immune Joel skeptical  of this Revelation goes along with  transporting her anyway it's the weapons  for him and he is absolutely no  attachment to this degenerate in his  eyes as their Journey continues Joel's  toughened exterior is only so tough  first blaming some of the mishaps on  Ellie's whole involvement like tests  being bitten on their way to meet the  fireflies but Joel never abandons Ellie  sure there is that quiet tough love  nature to him like when Joel is attacked  by a hunter in the hotel Ellie saves his  life with her knife he instantly is  pissed like a father disappointed in  going against his wishes but he soon  learns that Ellie isn't like Sarah she  is maybe a surrogate daughter in the  making but she is stubborn and holds her  own Joel slowly becomes more open with  Ellie alluding to his time as a hunter  talking about Sarah in a loving  memorable way even though it's been  roughly 20 years he still has this  fondness for his lost daughter while  also having reoccurring nightmares of  that night on outbreak day it's really  shown that Joel cares for Ellie like a  daughter when they finally meet up with  Tommy and the others in Wyoming Tommy  gives Joel an old picture of him and  Sarah after a soccer match however Joel  says that he's good showing that those  painful memories of Sarah are something  he wants to put in the rear view mirror  after Bandits attack the damn this is  where Joel's feelings towards Ellie  really shift consoling her asking if  she's okay something not necessarily  shown prior to this it's almost like  that picture of Sarah was his daughter  in a different time a different life and  now Ellie is his shot at a second chance  to have new memories with a daughter he  never got to share with before all of  this Joel was all about handing Ellie  off to a different party as their  responsibility completely forgetting her  but then after this run-in Joel finally  takes on the responsibility to deliver  Ellie to the fireflies it's that  father-daughter relationship that  blossoms and is reflected more so in the  future scenes with Joel trying to  explain like football to Ellie it's Joel  opening up about his hobbies and  passions to someone he cares about once  they arrive at the University in  Colorado only to discover the fireflies  have moved operations to Salt Lake City  there's this small glint of Hope in  Joel's tone that he won't have to end  the journey with Ellie just yet with  them becoming so close he doesn't really  want to pass her along however this is  all cut short as they are tacked by a  group of Bandits resulting in Joel  landing on a rogue piece of rebar  impaling his abdomen this injury almost  ends his life but Ellie is able to nurse  him back to health during the winter  months in a basement of an abandoned  house during this time the roles are  almost reversed where Ellie is the one  looking after Joel and this is the other  side of the coin showing now that the  pair is in for the Long Haul Elias  however captured by members of the same  Bandit group that attacked them at the  University learning that they are  cannibals led by a real creepy man by  the name of David now I won't get too  far into David but he is basically a  demented version of Joel who has  descended much further into the darkness  of this world completely warped so it's  really interesting Dynamic to introduce  him and how Ellie has to maneuver  interactions with this character in  order to locate Ellie Joel reverts to  his old Hunter days eliminating all but  two Bandits and interrogates the pair up  to this point we've seen Joel do some  gnarly things and hinted at a much  darker past but here we see a side of  this loving father that is a straight up  Sinister he's a man that will do  anything to get his daughter back or in  this case Ellie and straight up tortures  the pair it really speaks volumes of  Joel's character how much he has evolved  from even the start of he and Ellie's  journey and there is still that Primal  Rage in him but instantly shifts to  consoling Ellie when he finds her making  mincemeat of David Joel will do anything  for Ellie at this point which makes the  ending such a gut punch of an impact  Joel and Ellie eventually stumbled upon  the fireflies held up in an old hospital  in Salt Lake City advising Joel had made  it there just in time Ellie is being  prepared for surgery and finally a  potential cure can be researched to stop  the infection however when Joel  discovers that Ellie is being sacrificed  for the the procedure is Primal Rage  coupled with the loving father both come  out eliminating most of the fireflies  the doctors and takes Ellie back for  himself it's such a conflicting thing  for Joel to do because a heavy portion  of their Journey he just wants to leave  her on the side of the road and move on  with things but here he theoretically  Dooms Humanity for his own selfish  reasons in a way Joel saving Ellie and  then lying to her in the car ride back  to Wyoming is him wanting to create this  faux life for himself to live in  distracting himself from those  nightmares out there that Tommy had  mentioned earlier Joel is one heck of a  conflicted character at the end of this  he cares deeply for Ellie he wouldn't  let anything happen to her but yet lies  to her face about maybe the biggest  medical advancement in the past few  decades the ending really completes the  complex Journey Joel makes from the  beginning of the story initially Joel is  this loving father who seemingly would  sacrifice himself for his daughter  eventually evolving into someone who is  willing to sacrifice his friends and  finally metaphorically sacrifice all of  humanity for Ellie Troy Baker The Voice  talent for Joel added that in doing this  Joel robbed Ellie of her meaningful  sacrifice to save The Wider World from  the infection and so robbed her life of  a wider meaning because he believed if  we can't save one little world then it's  not a world worth saving Weeks Later  back at the Jackson Community in Wyoming  Joel is a bit conflicted about the  decision he made confiding in Tommy  about what really went down in Salt Lake  City the first thing Tommy asks is if he  told Ellie the truth instead lying that  there was no cure in order to protect  her Joel very much has morphed into a  full-on father figure towards her and  Tommy responds with wouldn't have done  it differently after hearing Joel's  reasoning Joel visits Ellie letting her  know how well she's integrating in with  the community and gives her the guitar  that he found Joel even shares his love  of music with her by playing Future Days  by Pearl Jam softly singing the lyrics  about future days and days of you and me  that resonate with Ellie as she listens  to Joel softly sing this is another key  moment because Joel finally shares his  talents with her again wanting to be  this loving father than giving the  guitar to her for her to learn a couple  years had passed as they fully integrate  into the Jackson Community Joel being  Tommy's brother became a well-known  trusted respected hard-working member in  the community mainly him and Tommy would  Patrol the Mountain View Lodge area  cleaning out infected one winter it was  said that the pair took out over 20  clickers and bloaters in a large horde  up on the mountain Joel continued to  care for Ellie like a daughter teaching  her how to play the guitar finally how  to swim and on her 16th birthday  surprised her by taking her to a nearby  museum Ellie loves museums by the way at  the Museum he surprised Ellie with not  only a model spaceship exhibit but also  a recording of the Apollo 11 launch  having Ellie imagined that she was  flying into space he gifted her a space  pendant to certify her as an official  astronaut roughly a year later Joel had  to finally confront Ellie about the  truth about what really happened all  those years ago at the hospital Ellie  went off to search for her own answers  with Joel reading a note that she had  left and then following her knowing he  couldn't keep this from her Joel admits  the fireflies indeed saw hope in Ellie  and were confident that Akira would be  developed but he intervened stopping  them to save her life this fractured  their relationship as Ellie was no  longer on speaking terms with Joel  sometime later Joel caused quite a stir  at the Jackson annual Winter Dance  trying to stick up for Ellie after  kissing her girlfriend Dina but this was  a bit too overbearing as he wasn't her  actual father and this caused  embarrassment later that night Ellie  confronted Joel playing his guitar on  his porch she scolded him for stealing  her true purpose in life with Joel  responding that if God had given him a  second chance he would have done the  same thing over again this affirmed his  love and care and selfishness towards  Ellie but also allowed them to slowly  rebuild their relationship on March 2nd  2038 Joel and Tommy got caught up in a  blizzard on a patrol saving a stranded  hiker named Abby Anderson as they escape  the weather and infected to a hideout at  the Baldwin Mansion where Abby's friends  were staying this was all a trap though  because once the two introduced  themselves the room fell silent and Abby  shot Joel in the leg they knocked out  Tommy and tied up Joel wrapping his leg  in a make shift tourniquet so he  wouldn't bleed out Joel urges them to do  whatever speech they have planned and  get it over with it's not revealed at  the time though but Abby is the daughter  of the doctor that Joel shot at the  hospital all those years ago to save