  Ellie Abby finally caught up to him to  get her revenge beating him with a  nearby Golf Club Ellie tries to save him  but Abby's group overpowers her holding  her down to watch Joel's Last Breath  pleading and threatening them Abby  Smashes in Joel's head ending his life  Ellie in a panic promises she's gonna  get her revenge but is knocked  unconscious Joel was 56 when he died and  was the closest thing to a father that  Ellie had it's an interesting parallel  of how Joel's Journey started with him  watching his daughter pass and then at  the end his new daughter Ellie watches  as he passes away Joel's body was later  buried in the Jackson Cemetery with  several member members of the community  leaving condolences outside of his house  Ellie never fully recovered from the  tragedy of watching Joel that day she  later had several moments of PTSD  reminding her of that nightmarish day  which affected her and drove her to get  even just like what Abby had set out to  do in the end one of the most  heartbreaking moments from the game is  Ellie trying to play Joel's guitar she  tries to play the same song Joel was  playing the night that she confronted  him about everything but after losing a  couple of fingers it's impossible for  her to strum the same tune without  messing up this small thing that  connected the two was also taken from  her as Ellie breaks down once again  leaving the guitar behind  honestly The Last of Us and last of us  too are the best video game stories I've  ever played I even got a bit emotional  during a couple moments from the second  game and that last guitar scene was  definitely one of them druckman and crew  did a great job of fleshing out these  characters especially Joel a man with a  clouded past some might even say a  villain in a certain point of view but  that doesn't stop him from being one of  the most complex well-developed video  game characters out there again part of  me would have absolutely done what he  did for Ellie obviously I'd love to hear  your thoughts on Joel did he do the  right things and what do you think of  Pedro Pascal's portrayal of the  character so far and I'll let you know  we're currently running the competition  giving away three copies of Black Adam  and Dawn of the Dead on the 15th of  January and all you gotta do to get a  chance of winning this is like this  video subscribe with notifications on  and drop your comments Down Below on the  last of us we pick the comments at  random at the end of every single month  and the winners of last month are on  screen right now so if that's you  message us on Twitter at heavy spoilers  if you want something else to watch be  sure to check out our Last of Us episode  1 breakdown Paul gets into everything it  is fantastic go check it out but with  that out of the way thank you as always  for watching I've been Jared I'll see in  the next one take care and peace
 

